#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The mempalace helper: read-only access to the owner's MemPalace for an agent.

It is one file that imports the standard library and the workbench kit (``wbkit``); the launcher runs a
private copy of it through the kit runner with nothing beside it.

    mempalace status
    mempalace search [--wing <name>] [--room <name>] [--results <1-20>] [--since <date>] [--before <date>]
                     -- <query>
    mempalace preview mine <dir> [--wing <name>] [--mode projects|convos] [--allow-project-root]
                                   (what mine would file, and a digest of it)
    mempalace mine <dir> [--confirm [--digest <digest>]] [--wing <name>] [--mode projects|convos]
                         [--allow-project-root]     (the owner, from a terminal, or at the level ask with a digest)
    mempalace preview sync <dir>                    (what sync would remove, and a digest of it)
    mempalace sync <dir> [--confirm [--digest <digest>]]    (the same two ways; the wing is the setting's or the default)

The contract is ``docs/specs/mempalace.md``. The helper starts the ``mempalace`` program, found on a PATH entry
outside the repository, with no shell, a fixed argument shape, a time limit, a cap on its output and an
environment built here. What the program prints is recalled data: it is cleaned, cut to a bound and printed
between two marker lines that carry a random token, and the helper never runs it or believes it. A search
never changes a stored drawer, but the program does rewrite its own index and bookkeeping files while it
searches (``docs/specs/mempalace.md``, "search"), and the helper refuses a search when the embedding model is
not already cached, so that an agent's search can never start a download.

``mine`` builds the palace. It is the owner's: the helper runs it only when standard input and output are
terminals, and then hands the terminal to the program (which prints progress), with no time limit; or, at the level
``ask``, with ``--confirm --digest <digest>`` and no terminal, when the digest is that of ``preview mine`` as it is
now, checked inside a lock, and then the program's output is captured and cut. It passes no
option that selects a language-model provider, a key, an endpoint, a daemon or a background job. There is no
``init``: the program's ``init`` writes ``mempalace.yaml`` and ``entities.json`` into the folder it scans (and, in
a git repository, appends to that folder's ``.gitignore``), and ``mine`` needs none of that. A project may name its palace in ``.workbench/local/mempalace.json``; the helper passes
it as ``--palace``.

``sync`` prunes the drawers of files that are gone or now ignored, from the one wing the setting names (or the default) and the one folder
given. It is the owner's in the same two ways as ``mine``, and it shares the lock, the digest check and the folder rules. Its default is the
program's dry run; ``--confirm`` makes it ``--apply``.
"""

